<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:45:15Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>India faces water and power stress after weak monsoon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48b42d31ff1aa6a5437a33693effb8fa5603d58bbf51d6869fa82d445127a756</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:44:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T14:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-faces-water-and-power-stress-after-weak-monsoon/a-79599540--95c0beffc2a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-faces-water-and-power-stress-after-weak-monsoon/a-79599540?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A weak monsoon is hitting farmers, water supplies and India's power system, while raising wider questions about increasingly erratic rainfall and its economic costs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea warns of AI-aided hacking after bank data breaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e08a3fb00d11fab9ad6aa90f08b75eba49fe7fc571485da120a827fc50fe243</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:44:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T12:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-warns-of-ai-aided-hacking-after-bank-data-breaches/a-79592922--3290ee11faa1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-warns-of-ai-aided-hacking-after-bank-data-breaches/a-79592922?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seoul is alarmed after a recent breach of South Korean banks' cyber defenses that reportedly involved AI-assisted hacking. Officials warn such methods could be used to also target other sectors and government agencies.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Security in the Black Sea region: is Bulgaria the weak link in Europe's defense against threats from Russia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:657832c7f45be7d07cc762a216730cc3eb19ff0a106587b66d30cf23fdc2834c</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:44:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T11:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/security-in-the-black-sea-region-is-bulgaria-the-weak-link-in-europe-s-defense-against-threats-from-/a-79592663--cd93d129d2db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/security-in-the-black-sea-region-is-bulgaria-the-weak-link-in-europe-s-defense-against-threats-from-russia/a-79592663?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two ships have sunk off the coast of Bulgaria and Romania after drone attacks in recent days. Bulgaria has held back on pointing the finger at Russia. What does that mean for security in the Black Sea and the region?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea recalls Ukraine ambassador amid POW dispute</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bcb622bdbe181b2d0a29f9c88e54fdcf4253202cbedd033de54b5b5d3ce38660</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:44:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-recalls-ukraine-ambassador-amid-pow-dispute/a-79590511--9732a38bcd21.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-recalls-ukraine-ambassador-amid-pow-dispute/a-79590511?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Korea has said it will recall its ambassador to Ukraine. Seoul is upset about a transfer of North Korean prisoners of war being made public knowledge at the UN and had demanded — but not received — an apology.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>As Russia steps up attacks on Ukrainian data centers, could Ukraine soon be offline?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c473aca3d6b1f02c78b1ab7b225a29810287cbc4183f4b914a79347dcb8f9dbc</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:45:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T10:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-russia-steps-up-attacks-on-ukrainian-data-centers-could-ukraine-soon-be-offline/a-79582503--ed9380350022.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-russia-steps-up-attacks-on-ukrainian-data-centers-could-ukraine-soon-be-offline/a-79582503?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Russia targets Ukraine's data centers more and more, experts say the country's internet system is too robust to shut down entirely. However, services could become more expensive.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Middle Corridor: Can Bulgaria be a safe gateway for Asian imports to the EU?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71b50f1b56b1bfbe37fa18ab34eb97140c455d8a172974d69db0c0cf590e3840</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:45:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T08:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/middle-corridor-can-bulgaria-be-a-safe-gateway-for-asian-imports-to-the-eu/a-79584530--0deecfdaf02f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/middle-corridor-can-bulgaria-be-a-safe-gateway-for-asian-imports-to-the-eu/a-79584530?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU wants more trade via the Middle Corridor, which could bring big benefits for Bulgaria. But Tuesday's drone attacks on commercial ships off the Bulgarian coast are a stark reminder of the security risks involved.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why music in Iran is more than just entertainment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec7fa1f87658d6675e55999608af12b74b0bc702998f228205997afd1ebc0535</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:43:29Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T05:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-music-in-iran-is-more-than-just-entertainment/a-79583224--67cbee1305a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-music-in-iran-is-more-than-just-entertainment/a-79583224?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iranian authorities are trying to persuade prominent singers in exile to return home. While the state seeks to harness music as a political tool, music has also become a powerful expression of dissent and resistance.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Sudan's road to elections remains uncertain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2851cb5f6e5a060738ce541d7ce9dd54acf8c1be928da509cea19c020bb4656a</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:43:29Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T04:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-sudan-s-road-to-elections-remains-uncertain/a-79563442--6016ef79f3a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-sudan-s-road-to-elections-remains-uncertain/a-79563442?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Sudan's first general election is set for December 22. Insecurity, political tensions and the failure to begin voter registration have raised doubts over whether a credible poll can be held.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>As US midterm elections loom, Trump's campaign tactics are becoming increasingly unusual, and expensive</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abd68a3a104fe1dd7d1db615f244fab01fd5d697de915082d6010c32c2512e9a</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:43:29Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T20:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-us-midterm-elections-loom-trump-s-campaign-tactics-are-becoming-increasingly-unusual-and-expensiv/a-79585673--1f3e5f62f0c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-us-midterm-elections-loom-trump-s-campaign-tactics-are-becoming-increasingly-unusual-and-expensive/a-79585673?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite not being on the ballot, Trump is campaigning hard ahead of the upcoming midterm elections. His tactics and promises have mostly been at the expense of US taypayers. Experts say some might violate federal law.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia, Pakistan, Turkey: Could the Mecca defense pact become a game changer in the war against the Houthis in Yemen?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20ebd3f3d2ec2c2515351b3ddb5137cec30947ad8831ef7801283c03d4c19001</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:43:29Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T17:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-pakistan-turkey-could-the-mecca-defense-pact-become-a-game-changer-in-the-war-against-t/a-79577245--88d642176557.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-pakistan-turkey-could-the-mecca-defense-pact-become-a-game-changer-in-the-war-against-the-houthis-in-yemen/a-79577245?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pakistan and Turkey have agreed to provide "practical measures" to defend Saudi Arabia against Houthi attacks. Could a new alliance reshape the war against the Houthis in Yemen?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Gerhard Schröder visits latest Russian employer, Hyperglobus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f53b41f7b6873f4586fb93f9cbe6500db9b85537386365af68d7e43736ae0f8f</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:43:29Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T16:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gerhard-schr_der-visits-latest-russian-employer-hyperglobus/a-79583018--1d88da466f5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gerhard-schröder-visits-latest-russian-employer-hyperglobus/a-79583018?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former German Chancellor Gerhard Schröder visited a Moscow supermarket in his new role on the supervisory board. Schröder is no stranger to retirement stipends in Russia — or the scandal that accompanies them.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU enlargement: European Commission tables reforms to prepare bloc for new members</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:22c0a1275f95a307402586250fb9638cc459ccc738c4d14141c9644e295539ef</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:43:29Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T15:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-european-commission-tables-reforms-to-prepare-bloc-for-new-members/a-79582493--0237e634d1b1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-european-commission-tables-reforms-to-prepare-bloc-for-new-members/a-79582493?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission is proposing earlier access to EU markets for candidate countries, new voting rules to reduce vetoes and extra safeguards for a bigger bloc. But is the reform fair — or even feasible?</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
